CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts _ --unwindset callee.0:4 --unwinding-assertions
^\[callee.assigns.\d+\] line \d+ Check that h is assignable: FAILURE$
^\[callee.assigns.\d+\] line \d+ Check that g\[.*0\] is assignable: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Check that a is assignable
Check that b is assignable
Check that k is assignable
--
Locals of a callee that are declared or assigned inside a loop without a
contract must not be checked against the write set of the caller's loop, while
the callee's writes to globals must still be checked against it. Unlike
loop_contracts_callee_with_loop, this test fails if checks inside the
uncontracted loop are suppressed altogether.
